WEBVTT

00:00:09.380 --> 00:00:10.610
Storm's coming.

00:00:10.610 --> 00:00:13.520
And you boys, you are
smack in the middle of it.

00:00:15.030 --> 00:00:19.240
Dad wants us to pick up where he left
off... saving people, hunting things.

00:00:21.230 --> 00:00:22.220
Family business.

00:00:22.220 --> 00:00:24.220
I'm gonna save as many people as we can.

00:00:25.240 --> 00:00:28.900
Dean, you and I have seen things
most people couldn't even dream about.

00:00:31.690 --> 00:00:32.920
If it's supernatural, we kill it.

00:00:32.920 --> 00:00:34.010
End of story. That's our job.

00:00:34.010 --> 00:00:35.460
No, Dean, that is not our job.

00:00:35.460 --> 00:00:36.860
Our job is hunting evil.

00:00:36.860 --> 00:00:38.320
They're all the same, Sam.

00:00:38.320 --> 00:00:39.860
They're not human, okay?

00:00:39.860 --> 00:00:41.730
We have to exterminate
every last one of them.

00:00:41.730 --> 00:00:43.450
Our lives are weird, man.

00:00:44.080 --> 00:00:45.410
You're telling me.

00:01:07.340 --> 00:01:08.760
We're lost.

00:01:08.760 --> 00:01:09.370
No.

00:01:09.370 --> 00:01:10.750
This is a short cut...

00:01:11.730 --> 00:01:15.860
Babe, it's just we've been on this road over
an hour, and we haven't seen a single car.

00:01:15.860 --> 00:01:18.240
Molly, I know how to
read a frickin' map, okay?

00:01:19.580 --> 00:01:21.160
We passed a gas station a while back.

00:01:21.160 --> 00:01:22.080
Let's just go ask someone.

00:01:22.080 --> 00:01:22.940
That was 40 minutes ago.

00:01:22.940 --> 00:01:24.080
We're not turning around.

00:01:24.080 --> 00:01:25.730
Come on.

00:01:25.730 --> 00:01:28.460
Isn't this argument a little archaic?

00:01:29.180 --> 00:01:30.970
Men can ask directions these days.

00:01:30.970 --> 00:01:31.790
No, we can't.

00:01:31.790 --> 00:01:33.030
It's against our genetic code.

00:01:33.030 --> 00:01:34.930
Look, I know exactly where we are.

00:01:34.930 --> 00:01:36.490
Oh, yeah? Where?

00:01:37.090 --> 00:01:38.380
Highway 99, okay?

00:01:38.380 --> 00:01:39.980
It cuts right through.

00:01:44.310 --> 00:01:46.110
Highway 99, huh?

00:01:50.240 --> 00:01:53.810
Okay, so we're taking the scenic route.

00:01:53.850 --> 00:01:55.480
David.

00:01:56.000 --> 00:01:58.890
It's our anniversary, and we're
spending it stuck in the car.

00:01:59.370 --> 00:01:59.970
I know.

00:01:59.970 --> 00:02:01.230
I'm sorry.

00:02:02.760 --> 00:02:04.670
Let me make it up to
you, okay? Come here.

00:02:04.920 --> 00:02:06.960
Stop. I'm mad at you.

00:02:07.280 --> 00:02:08.780
Oh, come on, Molly.

00:02:08.780 --> 00:02:11.210
Hey, you love me.

00:02:11.210 --> 00:02:12.450
No, I don't.

00:02:12.450 --> 00:02:14.070
You're a jerk.

00:02:16.430 --> 00:02:18.090
David, I mean it.

00:02:18.200 --> 00:02:19.150
Molly!

00:02:56.180 --> 00:02:57.400
David?

00:03:02.410 --> 00:03:03.640
David?

00:03:08.300 --> 00:03:09.490
David?

00:03:23.590 --> 00:03:24.970
David?

00:03:31.000 --> 00:03:32.850
Da... David?!

00:03:42.680 --> 00:03:44.110
David?!

00:03:49.590 --> 00:03:50.910
David?

00:04:16.660 --> 00:04:17.730
Hello?

00:04:19.430 --> 00:04:20.830
Is anyone here?

00:04:23.750 --> 00:04:25.180
Hello?

00:04:43.650 --> 00:04:44.860
It's you.

00:04:45.600 --> 00:04:46.330
You're okay.

00:04:46.630 --> 00:04:47.520
I'm so sorry.

00:04:47.520 --> 00:04:48.930
I didn't see you there.

00:04:49.790 --> 00:04:50.540
Are you...

00:04:51.300 --> 00:04:52.270
Are you hurt?

00:04:53.850 --> 00:04:54.910
Sir?

00:05:34.210 --> 00:05:37.150
Stop!

00:05:43.940 --> 00:05:45.350
You've got to help me.

00:05:47.410 --> 00:05:48.180
Please.

00:05:48.180 --> 00:05:49.150
Please!

00:05:49.150 --> 00:05:49.800
All right, all right.

00:05:49.800 --> 00:05:51.250
Calm down, calm down.

00:05:51.470 --> 00:05:52.490
Tell us what happened.

00:05:52.490 --> 00:05:54.890
I-I swerved,
a-And we crashed.

00:05:54.890 --> 00:06:00.060
And when I came to, the car was
wrecked and my husband was missing.

00:06:01.180 --> 00:06:05.060
I went looking for him, but that's when the
man from the road, he... he started chasing me.

00:06:05.680 --> 00:06:09.170
Did he look like he lost
a fight with a lawn mower?

00:06:09.820 --> 00:06:11.230
How did you know that?

00:06:12.590 --> 00:06:13.760
Lucky guess.

00:06:14.920 --> 00:06:17.070
Ma'am, what's your name?

00:06:17.070 --> 00:06:18.180
Molly.

00:06:18.510 --> 00:06:20.000
Molly Mcnamara.

00:06:20.000 --> 00:06:22.160
I think maybe you should come with us.

00:06:22.160 --> 00:06:23.080
We'll take you back into town.

00:06:23.080 --> 00:06:24.280
I can't.

00:06:24.280 --> 00:06:25.430
I have to find David.

00:06:25.430 --> 00:06:26.790
He might have gone back to the car.

00:06:26.790 --> 00:06:28.410
We should get you somewhere safe first.

00:06:28.410 --> 00:06:29.830
Then Dean and I will come back.

00:06:29.830 --> 00:06:30.770
We'll look for your husband.

00:06:30.770 --> 00:06:31.230
No.

00:06:31.230 --> 00:06:33.390
I'm not leaving here without him.

00:06:36.800 --> 00:06:39.870
Would you just take me
back to my car, please?

00:06:42.410 --> 00:06:43.190
Of course.

00:06:43.240 --> 00:06:44.530
Come on.

00:07:05.360 --> 00:07:06.610
It's right over there.

00:07:12.390 --> 00:07:13.820
I don't understand.

00:07:14.590 --> 00:07:16.060
I'm sure this is where it was.

00:07:16.060 --> 00:07:17.980
W-We hit that tree right there.

00:07:18.890 --> 00:07:21.140
This... this doesn't make any sense.

00:07:24.930 --> 00:07:26.180
Dean, we got to get out of here.

00:07:26.410 --> 00:07:27.820
Greeley could show up at any second.

00:07:27.820 --> 00:07:28.630
What are you gonna tell her.

00:07:29.870 --> 00:07:30.730
The truth?

00:07:31.520 --> 00:07:33.630
She's gonna take off running
in the other direction.

00:07:34.050 --> 00:07:37.120
I know it sounds crazy, but
I crashed into that tree.

00:07:37.190 --> 00:07:38.500
I don't know who could've taken it.

00:07:38.500 --> 00:07:40.200
It was totaled.

00:07:42.520 --> 00:07:44.220
Please. You have to believe me.

00:07:45.270 --> 00:07:47.390
Molly, listen, we do believe you.

00:07:47.390 --> 00:07:49.520
But that's why we want
to get you out of here.

00:07:49.520 --> 00:07:51.240
What about David?

00:07:51.240 --> 00:07:52.450
Something must have happened.

00:07:52.450 --> 00:07:53.690
I have to get to the cops.

00:07:53.690 --> 00:07:55.150
Cops... that's a great idea.

00:07:55.150 --> 00:07:56.920
We'll take you down to
the station ourselves.

00:07:56.920 --> 00:07:59.130
So just come with us.

00:07:59.130 --> 00:08:01.690
It's the best way we can
help you and your husband.

00:08:05.540 --> 00:08:06.810
Okay.

00:08:15.840 --> 00:08:18.200
We're supposed to be in lake Tahoe.

00:08:18.670 --> 00:08:19.930
You and David?

00:08:20.460 --> 00:08:22.260
It's our five-Year anniversary.

00:08:22.810 --> 00:08:24.580
Hell of an anniversary.

00:08:25.940 --> 00:08:28.960
Right before, we were
having the dumbest fight.

00:08:30.790 --> 00:08:33.580
It was the only time we ever really
argued... when we were stuck in the car.

00:08:33.580 --> 00:08:34.840
Yeah.

00:08:35.120 --> 00:08:36.810
I know how that goes.

00:08:38.440 --> 00:08:40.380
You know the last thing I said to him?

00:08:42.150 --> 00:08:43.640
I called him a jerk.

00:08:44.750 --> 00:08:45.630
Oh, god.

00:08:47.780 --> 00:08:50.080
What if that's the last
thing I said to him?

00:08:51.370 --> 00:08:52.240
Molly...

00:08:53.210 --> 00:08:55.130
We're gonna figure out what
happened to your husband.

00:08:55.420 --> 00:08:56.620
I promise.

00:09:04.190 --> 00:09:06.520
Did you? No.

00:09:08.050 --> 00:09:10.440
I was afraid you'd say that.

00:09:13.270 --> 00:09:14.550
This song.

00:09:15.360 --> 00:09:16.200
What?

00:09:16.780 --> 00:09:19.400
It was playing when we crashed.

00:09:25.150 --> 00:09:26.510
She's mine.

00:09:27.370 --> 00:09:29.240
She's mine.

00:09:29.950 --> 00:09:30.960
She's mine.

00:09:30.960 --> 00:09:32.530
What is that?

00:09:37.220 --> 00:09:38.390
Hold on.

00:09:38.850 --> 00:09:40.560
What are you doing?

00:09:49.230 --> 00:09:50.120
What the...

00:09:51.630 --> 00:09:52.980
What the hell just happened?

00:09:52.980 --> 00:09:53.570
Don't worry, Molly.

00:09:53.570 --> 00:09:55.120
Everything's gonna be all right.

00:09:58.290 --> 00:10:00.370
Spoke a little too soon, Sammy.

00:10:21.310 --> 00:10:22.750
I don't think he's gonna let her leave.

00:10:32.810 --> 00:10:34.140
This can't be happening.

00:10:34.620 --> 00:10:35.350
Well...

00:10:36.400 --> 00:10:38.510
Trust me, it's happening.

00:10:50.550 --> 00:10:51.680
Well...

00:10:51.840 --> 00:10:52.900
Okay.

00:10:53.140 --> 00:10:55.870
Thanks for helping, but I think
I got it covered from here.

00:10:56.320 --> 00:10:56.830
Wait.

00:10:56.830 --> 00:10:57.730
Molly, Molly, wait a minute.

00:10:57.730 --> 00:10:58.780
Just leave me alone.

00:10:58.780 --> 00:10:59.980
No. Please. You have to listen to me.

00:10:59.980 --> 00:11:01.040
Just stay away.

00:11:01.400 --> 00:11:03.500
It wasn't a coincidence
that we found you, all right?

00:11:05.030 --> 00:11:06.190
What are you talking about?

00:11:06.300 --> 00:11:08.340
We weren't cruising for chicks
when we ran into you, sister.

00:11:08.340 --> 00:11:09.580
We were already out here.

00:11:09.860 --> 00:11:10.750
Hunting.

00:11:10.750 --> 00:11:12.660
Hunting for what?

00:11:14.620 --> 00:11:15.590
Ghosts.

00:11:17.350 --> 00:11:19.850
D... d... don't...

00:11:20.120 --> 00:11:21.760
Sugar coat it for her.

00:11:21.760 --> 00:11:23.060
You're nuts.

00:11:23.220 --> 00:11:24.220
Really?

00:11:24.290 --> 00:11:27.510
About as nuts as a vanishing
guy with his guts spilling out.

00:11:30.190 --> 00:11:31.380
You know what you saw.

00:11:39.790 --> 00:11:41.680
We think his name is Jonah Greeley.

00:11:42.940 --> 00:11:47.440
He was a local farmer that died
15 years ago on this highway.

00:11:47.530 --> 00:11:49.720
Just stop.

00:11:49.720 --> 00:11:54.460
One night a year, on the anniversary
of his death, he haunts this road.

00:11:55.710 --> 00:11:57.150
That's why we're here, Molly.

00:11:58.260 --> 00:11:59.490
To try and stop him.

00:12:00.520 --> 00:12:05.230
Now, I suppose this ghost
made my car disappear, too.

00:12:05.460 --> 00:12:06.800
Crazier things have happened.

00:12:06.800 --> 00:12:07.840
Huh?

00:12:08.640 --> 00:12:09.570
You know what?

00:12:10.000 --> 00:12:11.910
I'm all filled up on crazy.

00:12:11.910 --> 00:12:13.810
I'm gonna get the cops myself.

00:12:13.810 --> 00:12:16.340
I don't mean to be harsh, but I
don't think you're gonna get too far.

00:12:17.260 --> 00:12:18.630
What is that supposed to mean?

00:12:18.630 --> 00:12:20.890
Means that plan "a" was
trying to get you out of here.

00:12:20.890 --> 00:12:24.470
Obviously that didn't go over too
well with, uh, farmer road kill.

00:12:28.450 --> 00:12:29.880
Molly, we're telling the truth.

00:12:31.670 --> 00:12:33.870
Greeley's not gonna let
you leave this highway.

00:12:34.980 --> 00:12:40.260
You're s... you're serious
about this, aren't you?

00:12:40.780 --> 00:12:42.120
Deadly.

00:12:45.950 --> 00:12:49.370
Everyear, Greeley finds someone
to punish for what happened to him.

00:12:51.700 --> 00:12:53.270
Tonight that person is you.

00:12:53.440 --> 00:12:54.070
Why me?

00:12:54.070 --> 00:12:55.790
I didn't do anything.

00:12:55.790 --> 00:12:57.040
Doesn't matter.

00:12:58.750 --> 00:13:00.590
Some spirits only see what they want.

00:13:04.300 --> 00:13:08.560
So you're saying this
Greeley, he took my husband?

00:13:11.380 --> 00:13:12.470
Oh, god.

00:13:13.760 --> 00:13:15.810
Molly, look, we're
gonna help, all right?

00:13:18.040 --> 00:13:19.690
But first, you got to help us.

00:13:20.940 --> 00:13:22.100
Help you?

00:13:24.620 --> 00:13:25.670
How?

00:13:29.340 --> 00:13:29.910
This is it.

00:13:29.910 --> 00:13:31.390
This is where I saw him.

00:13:35.870 --> 00:13:37.250
Must have been his hunting cabin.

00:13:43.900 --> 00:13:45.440
Seemed like a real sweet guy.

00:13:49.540 --> 00:13:51.360
No markers or headstones outside.

00:13:51.540 --> 00:13:53.010
You're looking for Greeley's grave?

00:13:53.010 --> 00:13:53.980
Yeah.

00:13:54.250 --> 00:13:55.150
Why?

00:13:55.240 --> 00:13:57.520
So we can dig up the
corpse and salt and burn it.

00:13:58.350 --> 00:13:59.270
Oh.

00:13:59.630 --> 00:14:01.140
Sure. Naturally.

00:14:01.140 --> 00:14:02.990
It's a way to get rid of a spirit.

00:14:03.510 --> 00:14:04.920
And that'll save David?

00:14:04.920 --> 00:14:08.420
This is what'll help both of you,
provided there's a corpse to be found.

00:14:09.590 --> 00:14:10.700
So how do we find it?

00:14:10.700 --> 00:14:11.740
Uh, not sure.

00:14:11.740 --> 00:14:13.890
After Greeley died, his
wife claimed the body.

00:14:13.890 --> 00:14:15.660
And that was the last anyone saw of her.

00:14:15.660 --> 00:14:17.070
So good guess she brought him back here.

00:14:17.070 --> 00:14:18.880
But they have a thousand acres.

00:14:18.880 --> 00:14:20.910
He could be buried anywhere on 'em.

00:14:21.090 --> 00:14:22.660
Is is really what you guys do.

00:14:22.660 --> 00:14:24.180
You're like ghost busters.

00:14:24.180 --> 00:14:24.730
Yeah.

00:14:24.730 --> 00:14:25.810
Minus the jumpsuits.

00:14:25.810 --> 00:14:27.840
This is a fascinating
conversation and all.

00:14:27.840 --> 00:14:31.140
But this highway is only haunted once a year,
and we got till sun up to wrap this thing up.

00:14:31.140 --> 00:14:32.880
What do you say we move it along, okay?

00:14:32.880 --> 00:14:34.510
Great.

00:14:45.240 --> 00:14:46.670
What are we looking for?

00:14:46.670 --> 00:14:48.040
Greeley's house.

00:14:48.120 --> 00:14:49.630
Maybe he's buried there.

00:14:49.740 --> 00:14:51.480
Look for roads or paths or something.

00:14:51.480 --> 00:14:52.530
Stay close.

00:14:52.530 --> 00:14:53.010
Yeah.

00:14:53.010 --> 00:14:54.380
Okay.

00:15:01.100 --> 00:15:02.320
Molly?

00:15:03.760 --> 00:15:05.190
Molly, help me.

00:15:06.190 --> 00:15:07.440
Molly?

00:15:11.660 --> 00:15:14.090
David? David?

00:15:20.970 --> 00:15:22.580
Whoops.

00:15:28.580 --> 00:15:29.360
Hey!

00:15:29.360 --> 00:15:30.310
Are you all right?

00:15:30.310 --> 00:15:32.110
What has that son of a
bit chdone with my husband?

00:15:32.110 --> 00:15:34.720
Just take it easy, all right?

00:15:34.720 --> 00:15:36.050
You're gonna see David again.

00:15:36.050 --> 00:15:36.840
You will.

00:15:36.840 --> 00:15:38.060
Hey.

00:15:39.330 --> 00:15:40.960
Follow the creepy brick road.

00:15:42.760 --> 00:15:44.610
Go ahead.

00:15:57.080 --> 00:15:58.860
That thing shoots rock salt?

00:15:59.450 --> 00:16:00.300
Yep.

00:16:00.610 --> 00:16:02.880
And plain salt keeps away spirits?

00:16:03.730 --> 00:16:05.470
Simple remedies are always the best.

00:16:05.910 --> 00:16:10.710
In most cultures, salt is a symbol of purity,
so it repels impure and unnatural things.

00:16:10.710 --> 00:16:12.890
Same reason you throw
it over your shoulder.

00:16:18.230 --> 00:16:21.190
You know, just once I'd like to
round the corner and see a nice house.

00:16:56.760 --> 00:16:57.980
Any headstones outside?

00:16:57.980 --> 00:16:58.780
Yeah, right.

00:16:58.780 --> 00:17:00.160
Is it ever that easy?

00:17:00.160 --> 00:17:01.910
I guess not.

00:17:12.130 --> 00:17:13.180
You two check upstairs.

00:17:13.180 --> 00:17:15.580
See if you can find any notes or
records telling us where he's buried.

00:17:15.580 --> 00:17:16.860
I'll just check down here.

00:17:44.620 --> 00:17:45.670
Great.

00:18:10.320 --> 00:18:11.260
Look at this.

00:18:16.270 --> 00:18:18.110
It's Greeley and his wife.

00:18:38.200 --> 00:18:39.840
It's a love letter he wrote her.

00:18:41.800 --> 00:18:43.510
My god, it's beautiful.

00:18:47.730 --> 00:18:51.860
I don't understand how a guy like
this can turn into that monster.

00:18:56.160 --> 00:18:58.300
Spirits like Greeley are,uh...

00:18:59.640 --> 00:19:01.140
Like wounded animals.

00:19:02.330 --> 00:19:03.480
Lost.

00:19:04.710 --> 00:19:07.760
In so much pain, that they lash out.

00:19:08.420 --> 00:19:08.810
Why?

00:19:08.810 --> 00:19:10.090
Why are they here?

00:19:10.600 --> 00:19:12.570
Well, there's some part of them that...

00:19:13.490 --> 00:19:14.880
That's keeping them here.

00:19:16.210 --> 00:19:18.420
Like their remains or, um...

00:19:21.020 --> 00:19:22.280
Unfinished business.

00:19:22.980 --> 00:19:24.410
Unfinished business?

00:19:25.970 --> 00:19:26.700
Yeah.

00:19:28.740 --> 00:19:29.850
It could be revenge.

00:19:30.000 --> 00:19:31.780
Could be love.

00:19:32.460 --> 00:19:33.160
Or hate.

00:19:35.210 --> 00:19:37.630
Whatever it is, they
just hold on too tight.

00:19:39.080 --> 00:19:40.460
Can't let go.

00:19:41.200 --> 00:19:42.170
So they're trapped.

00:19:44.340 --> 00:19:45.990
Caught in the same loops.

00:19:47.770 --> 00:19:50.450
Replaying the same
tragedies over and over.

00:19:50.930 --> 00:19:52.760
You sound almost sorry for them.

00:19:53.060 --> 00:19:55.400
Well, they weren't
evil people, you know?

00:19:56.570 --> 00:19:57.640
A lot of them were good.

00:19:57.660 --> 00:19:59.020
Just...

00:20:00.290 --> 00:20:01.490
Something happened to them.

00:20:02.830 --> 00:20:04.620
Something they couldn't control.

00:20:06.300 --> 00:20:09.650
Sammy's always getting a little J. Love
Hewitt when it comes to things like this.

00:20:11.820 --> 00:20:13.940
Me, I don't like 'em.

00:20:14.170 --> 00:20:16.190
And I sure as hell ain't
making apologies for 'em.

00:20:19.640 --> 00:20:20.650
There's nothing downstairs.

00:20:23.000 --> 00:20:26.320
Uh, just about every piece of
mail or receipt they ever had.

00:20:27.230 --> 00:20:29.760
Looked through a couple, but
nothing about a grave so far.

00:20:34.000 --> 00:20:34.870
What?

00:20:35.000 --> 00:20:36.350
There's something behind here.

00:20:37.350 --> 00:20:38.240
Here.

00:20:53.850 --> 00:20:55.380
It's locked from the inside.

00:21:20.570 --> 00:21:22.190
Smells like old lady in here.

00:21:31.400 --> 00:21:32.660
And that would explain why.

00:21:38.740 --> 00:21:41.230
Well, now we know why
nobody ever saw her again.

00:21:41.230 --> 00:21:43.120
She didn't want to live without him.

00:21:49.050 --> 00:21:50.160
Dean, give me a hand.

00:21:52.660 --> 00:21:53.520
Really?

00:21:56.500 --> 00:21:57.500
What are you gonna do?

00:22:00.230 --> 00:22:01.720
We can't leave her like this.

00:22:01.720 --> 00:22:02.840
Why not?

00:22:03.070 --> 00:22:04.980
She deserves to be put to rest, Dean.

00:22:16.480 --> 00:22:17.330
So...

00:22:22.130 --> 00:22:25.210
So, if you manage to put
Greeley to rest, too...

00:22:26.520 --> 00:22:27.920
What happens to them?

00:22:29.640 --> 00:22:32.100
Lady, that answer is
way beyond our pay grade.

00:22:32.300 --> 00:22:34.920
You hunt these things, but you
don't know what happens to them?

00:22:35.290 --> 00:22:36.440
Well, they never come back.

00:22:36.440 --> 00:22:37.910
That's all that matters.

00:22:41.080 --> 00:22:43.810
After they let go of
whatever'skeeping them here, they...

00:22:44.930 --> 00:22:45.970
They just go.

00:22:47.050 --> 00:22:49.580
I hope someplace better,
but we don't know.

00:22:51.120 --> 00:22:52.390
No one does.

00:22:52.460 --> 00:22:54.310
What happens when you burn their bones?

00:22:55.180 --> 00:23:00.530
Well, my dad used to say that was
like death for ghosts, you know?

00:23:00.830 --> 00:23:01.950
But...

00:23:02.330 --> 00:23:04.280
The truth is, we still don't know.

00:23:04.970 --> 00:23:06.420
Not for sure.

00:23:10.420 --> 00:23:13.280
Guess that's why we all
hold on to life so hard.

00:23:14.820 --> 00:23:16.050
Even the dead.

00:23:17.670 --> 00:23:19.570
We're all just scared of the unknown.

00:23:20.570 --> 00:23:22.750
The only thing I'm
scared of is losing David.

00:23:25.100 --> 00:23:26.600
I have to see him again.

00:23:38.250 --> 00:23:39.840
I have to.

00:24:06.590 --> 00:24:08.300
I think we should tell
her about her husband.

00:24:08.470 --> 00:24:09.360
We can't.

00:24:11.610 --> 00:24:14.990
Dean, it's cruel, letting
her pine for him like this.

00:24:14.990 --> 00:24:16.470
I don't like keeping her in the dark.

00:24:16.470 --> 00:24:17.730
It's for her own good.

00:24:23.680 --> 00:24:26.440
I know you feel guilty,
butlet's just stick to the plan.

00:24:26.640 --> 00:24:27.430
Let's get her out of here.

00:24:27.430 --> 00:24:28.280
Then we'll tell her.

00:24:28.280 --> 00:24:29.440
Tell me what?

00:24:31.870 --> 00:24:33.570
What aren't you telling me?

00:24:36.890 --> 00:24:37.600
It's about David.

00:24:37.600 --> 00:24:39.260
You know what happened to him.

00:24:39.800 --> 00:24:41.240
Molly Sam, don't.

00:24:41.260 --> 00:24:42.400
Don't what?

00:24:43.590 --> 00:24:46.210
Don't tell me because
I'll mess up your hunt?

00:24:46.270 --> 00:24:49.040
You don't care about me or my husband.

00:24:49.040 --> 00:24:50.370
That's not true.

00:24:50.370 --> 00:24:51.440
Really?

00:24:53.130 --> 00:24:55.490
Then whatever it is, tell me, please.

00:25:04.260 --> 00:25:05.280
He's coming.

00:25:07.040 --> 00:25:08.000
Stay with her...

00:26:16.200 --> 00:26:17.280
He's got Molly!

00:26:42.950 --> 00:26:44.220
This guy is persistent.

00:26:44.410 --> 00:26:45.450
We got to find Molly.

00:26:45.600 --> 00:26:46.930
We got to find Greeley's bones.

00:26:46.930 --> 00:26:51.550
And, uh, no pressure or anything, but we
got less than two hours before sunrise.

00:26:53.040 --> 00:26:53.940
Hey.

00:26:55.100 --> 00:26:56.010
What do you got?

00:26:57.730 --> 00:26:59.710
"February 6, 1992. "

00:27:00.230 --> 00:27:02.040
That was like two weeks
before the accident, wasn't it?

00:27:02.040 --> 00:27:02.860
Yeah.

00:27:02.860 --> 00:27:04.810
It looks like the hunting cabin, but...

00:27:05.360 --> 00:27:08.440
I swear there's a tree there
right where they're standing.

00:27:12.220 --> 00:27:13.340
Should have thought of it.

00:27:13.340 --> 00:27:14.450
What?

00:27:14.450 --> 00:27:15.830
It's an old country custom, Dean.

00:27:15.830 --> 00:27:17.970
Planting a tree as a grave marker.

00:27:19.650 --> 00:27:22.580
You're like a walking
encyclopedia of weirdness.

00:27:24.920 --> 00:27:25.630
Yeah.

00:27:25.630 --> 00:27:26.780
I know.

00:27:28.560 --> 00:27:29.770
Where's David?

00:27:30.800 --> 00:27:31.980
What did you do to him?

00:27:33.830 --> 00:27:36.190
You shouldn't worry about him anymore.

00:27:37.060 --> 00:27:38.320
Oh, my god.

00:27:38.490 --> 00:27:40.860
You should worry about yourself.

00:27:41.880 --> 00:27:43.420
I didn't do anything to you.

00:27:43.560 --> 00:27:44.640
Oh?

00:27:47.740 --> 00:27:49.990
I know... I know about your wife.

00:27:50.760 --> 00:27:52.830
Hurting me won't bring her back.

00:27:54.770 --> 00:27:56.370
My wife is gone.

00:27:59.560 --> 00:28:03.330
All I got left'shurting you.

00:28:11.770 --> 00:28:13.790
P-Please.

00:28:13.790 --> 00:28:15.430
Just let me go.

00:28:15.600 --> 00:28:16.610
Go?

00:28:18.130 --> 00:28:19.300
You're not gonna leave.

00:28:20.220 --> 00:28:22.590
You're never gonna leave.

00:28:33.360 --> 00:28:34.450
Go get Molly.

00:28:47.730 --> 00:28:48.710
Oh, thank god.

00:28:49.500 --> 00:28:50.700
Call me Dean.

00:28:58.660 --> 00:29:00.200
This guy's really pissing me off.

00:30:20.160 --> 00:30:22.040
Oh, baby, it's been a long night.

00:30:27.630 --> 00:30:28.360
All right.

00:30:30.500 --> 00:30:31.980
Let's get you out of here.

00:30:32.690 --> 00:30:36.750
I'm not going anywhere until you
tell me what happened to my husband.

00:30:38.010 --> 00:30:38.850
Molly...

00:30:39.030 --> 00:30:43.330
All this time I've been looking
for him, and you knew that...

00:30:44.430 --> 00:30:46.330
You knew that Greeley
killed him, didn't you?

00:30:49.620 --> 00:30:50.500
He's dead.

00:30:52.200 --> 00:30:53.250
No, Molly.

00:30:54.930 --> 00:30:56.520
David's alive.

00:30:56.950 --> 00:30:57.690
What?

00:30:59.470 --> 00:31:00.510
You're sure?

00:31:01.740 --> 00:31:02.840
I'm sure.

00:31:04.860 --> 00:31:05.650
We'll take you to him.

00:31:05.650 --> 00:31:06.870
Come on.

00:31:27.160 --> 00:31:29.260
He's in that house right there.

00:31:31.300 --> 00:31:32.380
I don't understand.

00:31:33.850 --> 00:31:34.820
You will.

00:31:54.750 --> 00:31:56.690
That's not...

00:32:01.240 --> 00:32:02.360
It can't be.

00:32:11.570 --> 00:32:12.930
What's happening?

00:32:15.740 --> 00:32:16.770
Who is that?

00:32:19.070 --> 00:32:20.530
That's David's wife.

00:32:28.580 --> 00:32:30.060
I'm sorry, Molly.

00:32:32.310 --> 00:32:36.640
15 years ago, you and your husband
it Jonah Greeley with your car.

00:32:40.480 --> 00:32:42.000
What are you saying?

00:32:42.880 --> 00:32:45.940
We're saying there isn't just
one spirit haunting highway 41.

00:32:45.940 --> 00:32:47.250
There are two.

00:32:48.050 --> 00:32:50.110
Jonah Greeley and you.

00:32:50.550 --> 00:32:54.820
For the past 15 years, one night a year
you've been appearing on that highway.

00:32:54.820 --> 00:32:56.570
No. That's not possible.

00:32:57.320 --> 00:33:00.330
It was our anniversary...
February 22nd...

00:33:00.330 --> 00:33:01.830
1992.

00:33:01.830 --> 00:33:02.890
Yes.

00:33:02.890 --> 00:33:05.360
Molly, it's 2007.

00:33:09.910 --> 00:33:11.240
Oh, god.

00:33:11.390 --> 00:33:13.090
All right. Tell me about highway 41.

00:33:13.090 --> 00:33:15.240
12 accidents over 15 years.

00:33:15.240 --> 00:33:18.150
Five of them fatal, all of them
happening on the same night.

00:33:18.150 --> 00:33:20.100
So what are we looking
at... interstate dead zone?

00:33:20.100 --> 00:33:21.310
Phantom hitchhiker? What?

00:33:21.310 --> 00:33:22.250
Not quite.

00:33:22.600 --> 00:33:25.420
Year after year, witnesses said
the same thing made 'em crash

00:33:25.420 --> 00:33:30.800
A woman appearing in the middle of the
road being chased by a man covered in blood.

00:33:30.800 --> 00:33:32.100
Two spooks?

00:33:46.650 --> 00:33:48.170
Now, where is Molly buried?

00:33:48.600 --> 00:33:51.170
She... she wasn't buried anywhere.

00:33:51.990 --> 00:33:53.330
She was cremated.

00:33:55.820 --> 00:33:57.640
So much for burning her bones.

00:33:57.690 --> 00:33:59.570
Yeah, but then what's keeping her here?

00:34:09.600 --> 00:34:11.490
Some spirits only see what they want.

00:34:12.590 --> 00:34:13.950
David?!

00:34:14.420 --> 00:34:15.450
David?

00:34:16.410 --> 00:34:17.140
Stop!

00:34:18.160 --> 00:34:19.600
Stop!

00:34:26.280 --> 00:34:27.800
You have to help me.

00:34:28.070 --> 00:34:29.960
Dean, I don't think
she knows she's dead.

00:34:33.460 --> 00:34:34.180
Please!

00:34:34.700 --> 00:34:35.270
Open up!

00:34:35.270 --> 00:34:35.690
Please!

00:34:35.690 --> 00:34:36.590
Okay. All right, all right.

00:34:36.590 --> 00:34:37.370
Just calm down.

00:34:37.370 --> 00:34:38.460
Tell us what happened.

00:34:38.530 --> 00:34:39.590
What are you gonna tell her?

00:34:40.510 --> 00:34:41.630
The truth.

00:34:42.210 --> 00:34:44.280
She's gonna take off running
in the other direction.

00:34:45.400 --> 00:34:47.280
Some spirits hold on too tight.

00:34:48.690 --> 00:34:49.900
Can't let go.

00:34:55.390 --> 00:34:56.400
And Greeley?

00:34:56.550 --> 00:35:01.560
Each year he punishes somebody
for his death... chasing them.

00:35:02.890 --> 00:35:04.410
Torturing them.

00:35:06.900 --> 00:35:10.950
And each year, that somebody is you.

00:35:11.210 --> 00:35:13.080
But I don't remember any of it.

00:35:13.240 --> 00:35:15.210
Because you couldn't
see the truth, Molly.

00:35:18.680 --> 00:35:23.100
So that's why he won't
let me off the highway.

00:35:25.380 --> 00:35:26.350
Because...

00:35:27.590 --> 00:35:29.120
I killed him.

00:35:31.510 --> 00:35:33.220
I killed us both.

00:35:40.440 --> 00:35:42.930
Why didn't you tell me
when you first saw me?

00:35:43.690 --> 00:35:45.260
Why wait until now?

00:35:45.670 --> 00:35:46.980
You wouldn't have believed us.

00:35:48.390 --> 00:35:49.870
And you needed me for bait.

00:35:52.590 --> 00:35:54.010
Well, we needed you.

00:35:57.560 --> 00:35:58.630
David.

00:35:58.890 --> 00:36:01.410
Molly, we brought you
here so you could move on.

00:36:02.380 --> 00:36:03.920
I have to tell him.

00:36:08.610 --> 00:36:09.560
That you love him?

00:36:10.320 --> 00:36:11.780
That you're sorry?

00:36:13.010 --> 00:36:15.010
Molly, he already knows that.

00:36:17.590 --> 00:36:20.130
Look, if you want to go in
there, we're not gonna stop you.

00:36:20.130 --> 00:36:22.460
Yeah, but you are gonna
freak him right out.

00:36:24.890 --> 00:36:26.020
For life.

00:36:36.730 --> 00:36:38.870
David's already said
his good byes, Molly.

00:36:39.490 --> 00:36:40.790
Now it's your turn.

00:36:41.560 --> 00:36:44.180
This is your unfinished business.

00:36:45.370 --> 00:36:47.090
What am I supposed to do?

00:36:49.650 --> 00:36:50.530
Just...

00:36:52.090 --> 00:36:52.960
Let go.

00:36:54.700 --> 00:36:55.700
Of David.

00:36:55.850 --> 00:36:57.260
Of everything.

00:36:58.520 --> 00:36:59.730
You do that...

00:37:00.960 --> 00:37:02.490
We think you'll move on.

00:37:03.880 --> 00:37:05.630
But you don't know where.

00:37:07.930 --> 00:37:09.160
No.

00:37:10.850 --> 00:37:12.750
Molly, you don't belong here.

00:37:14.000 --> 00:37:15.980
Haven't you suffer edlong enough?

00:37:18.560 --> 00:37:19.810
It's time.

00:37:21.670 --> 00:37:23.240
It's time to go.

00:38:12.610 --> 00:38:14.190
I guess she wasn't so bad...

00:38:14.930 --> 00:38:16.040
For a ghost.

00:38:18.920 --> 00:38:20.810
You think she's really
going to a better place?

00:38:22.470 --> 00:38:23.630
I hope so.

00:38:25.760 --> 00:38:26.910
I guess we'll never know.

00:38:26.910 --> 00:38:29.070
Not until we take the
plunge ourselves, huh?

00:38:30.190 --> 00:38:31.450
Doesn't really matter, Dean.

00:38:33.720 --> 00:38:35.450
Hope's kind of the whole point.

00:38:38.820 --> 00:38:40.100
All right, Haley Joel.

00:38:41.740 --> 00:38:43.060
Let's hit the road.

00:00:09.500 --> 00:00:11.000
<font color="#ffff00" size=14>www.tvsubtitles.net</font>
